+# Agent Note: Durable request-local message selection
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-17-request-message-selection.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Consumers need to choose model input without deleting execution history. Reusing transcript replacement or history selection for that choice would alter Chat, Trajectory and audit readers.
+
+## Decision
+
+A required request/messages event stores ordered original-event references and inline messages, with an optional earlier request base. Session resolves that record independently of its transcript. The generic agent/request-messages waterfall runs after existing admission and header recording; providers confirm persistence before returning a record sequence. The Loop and reconstruction invariant share the resolver. Ordinary consumers retain selected-history derivation.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+Intercepting llm/stream parameters would bypass durable reconstruction. Permanent injected messages would conflate per-call input with transcript facts. Copying every expanded historical message into every record would duplicate immutable content. A separate log would split request evidence from the Session that owns it.
+
+## Consequences
+
+References cannot point forward or to non-message events. Inline messages retain producer identity. Base records support stable continuation prefixes, but consumers own their grouping and retention policy. History selection never rewrites recorded requests. Token estimation can price exact assembled messages and tools independently of cumulative usage. Chat renderers can open a named inspection view without selecting execution history.
+
+The request event is required for replay, with no structural Session version change or released-validator rewrite. Session, Loop and scope tests cover resolution and dispatch; a recorded request-context scenario exercises ordinary and SDK projection. [History selection](2026-09-16-history-selection.md) continues to own transcript visibility.
