 <a id="model-experience"></a>
+## Selected execution history
+
+<a id="selected-execution-history"></a>
+
+history/selected stores ordered, disjoint inclusive raw-event ranges and a consecutive selection version. Every reference precedes the selection. It changes derived history, not raw records, lifecycle counters or usage. Subsequent events extend that selected history until another selection. Required event registration prevents unaware readers from silently treating all alternatives as one history.
+
+Session.readHistory returns a stable selected read with its selection version and raw high-water position. Surface, request-header and context reconstruction use the same selection. Reconstruct a historical request from its original raw prefix, not from today's selected read. The [history-selection decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-16-history-selection.md) explains these separate reads.
+
+## Request-local messages
+
+request/messages records an ordered selection of original event messages and inline producer messages. A record may cite an earlier request as its base; references must precede their containing record. A null selection restores ordinary history derivation. deriveRequestMessages resolves the current or explicitly selected record without changing the transcript surface. Original roles, content blocks, identities and provider replay data are preserved. The required event is independent of history/selected, so later history changes cannot alter an earlier request. [The decision](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-09-17-request-message-selection.md) explains the separate ownership.
+
